: Which brings up an interesting point.  How are stats computed?  Are they
: independantly random, or does a good dex make a bad int more likely?
: A spoiler on how each class computes stats would be most helpful.

Spoilers ahead!




























The initial statistics for different classes are computed as follows:

1.      75 points are divided between the six attributes based on
        the following table:


                STR     DEX     CON     INT     WIS     CHR

Archeologist     7      10      10       7       7       7
                20      20      20      10      20      10

Barbarian       16       7       7      15      16       6
                30       6       7      20      30       7

Caveman         10       7       7       7       8       6
                30       6       7      20      30       7

Elf             13      13      13       9      13       7
                30      10      10      20      20      10

Healer           7       7      13       7      11      16
                15      20      20      15      25      10

Knight          13       7      14       8      10      17
                20      15      15      10      20      10

Priest           7       7      10       7       7       7
                15      10      30      15      20      10

Rogue            7       7       7      10       7       6
                20      10      10      30      20      10

Samurai         10       8       7      10      17       6
                30      10      10      30      14      10

Tourist          7      10       6       7       7      10
                15      10      10      15      30      20

Valkyrie        10       7       7       7      10       7

Wizard           7      10       7       7       7       7
                10      30      10      20      20      10

        The first row tells the minimum value for the attributes.
        Rest of the points are distributed between the six attributes
        using the second row as precentage probabilities between
        different attributes.

        So for example elf gets at least 13/13/13/9/13/7, the sum of
        those attributes is 68, so 7 points are distibuted using
        30% / 10% / 10% / 20% / 20% / 10% as probabilities between
        the attributes.

        No attribute can go over the maximum.


2.      For every attribute the is 5% chance that it is further adjusted
        -2 .. +4 points. No attribute will be adjusted over maximum or
        under 3.

3.      Last thing is to adjust the strength upwards so that the character
        can carry its initial inventory.


